Package: fcitx5-zh-doctor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: fcitx5-zh-doctor <noreply@example.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: fcitx5, fcitx5-chinese-addons, fcitx5-pinyin, fcitx5-module-cloudpinyin,
 fcitx5-config-qt, fcitx5-frontend-gtk3, fcitx5-frontend-gtk4, fcitx5-frontend-qt5,
 libime-bin, fonts-arphic-ukai, xz-utils
Recommends: im-config, fcitx5-material-color
Description: ready-to-use fcitx5 Chinese input preset for Ubuntu/Debian
 Installs a working Chinese input setup for fcitx5:
  * Material green theme with a Kai (UKai) font
  * cloud pinyin configured for the Google CN backend
  * zh.wikipedia dictionary, compiled at install time against the
    libime version present on the target machine
 .
 The package exists because several defaults shipped by older fcitx5
 versions are broken: the Baidu cloud backend points at a dead
 endpoint, cloud pinyin is disabled by default, and prebuilt
 dictionaries fail to load with "Invalid pinyin version".
